  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+1y+(-1)z=1 \\\\ 1x+(-2)y+2z=3 \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+1z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-(-4))-(3-4)-(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & =2+1+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{5}{5}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
